{
	"id": "promises-are-eager",
	"text": "What went wrong? Ah, yes. That perfidious Promise. A Promise is not lazy. In fact, it is what the programming linguists call eager. It kicks off the moment it is defined. And once it resolves, either successfully or catastrophically, it will forever hold this initial value. Thus, when it was awaited a second time on the day of your unexpected demise, it did not procure a fresh reading, but instead regurgitated yesterday's value.",
